{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And armed they went up, etc.</b> It may be that, besides being armed with weapons, HaShem's leading them around so they would not retreat upon seeing war would avail nothing, for in any case they would return to Egypt since they had no weapons to engage the enemy in battle and would see themselves as lost. Therefore it says <b>and armed they went up</b>, etc. — meaning, besides the reason that HaShem led them around, they also had weapons, and by the combination of both reasons <b>the people would not have second thoughts upon seeing war, etc.</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:33.044502883Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}